From ad5c8cd6a4dc55a0b5ce194fcdebf1e62cad444c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Talaria <324092415+talaria0101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 05:38:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] ci: keep the attach-p-eperm tests on the ptrace backend;
 whitespace and coverage gates

* src/strace.c (init): do not fall back to the seccomp backend when
  -p/--attach is given -- the backend cannot attach to a running
  process, so stay on the ptrace backend and let the attach attempt
  produce its genuine error (and the yama hint).  Restores
  tests/attach-p-eperm-yama.test, broken by the backend selection
  change: the test disables ptrace for the traced strace and greps the
  attach error that the fallback's help message replaced.
* .gitattributes: exempt patches/series/*.patch (diff context is
  "space before tab" by construction) and experiments/logs/** (captured
  tool output contains tab-only lines) from whitespace error checks;
  the whitespace job checks the whole tree and our sources are clean.
* .github/workflows/ci.yml: do not fail the coverage job on the codecov
  upload -- this repository is not registered on Codecov, so the OIDC
  upload answers "Repository not found"; the coverage build still gates.
* docs/reviews/REVIEW-5.md: pass D (CI triage) documented.
* doc/strace.1.in: document that -p disables the seccomp fallback.
---
 .gitattributes                        |  7 +++++++
 .github/workflows/ci.yml              |  5 ++++-
 doc/strace.1.in                       |  5 ++++-
 docs/reviews/REVIEW-5.md              |  9 +++++++++
 experiments/logs/40-option-wiring.log |  2 +-
 src/strace.c                          | 11 ++++++++++-
 6 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index d4eba3a9c..357a8d033 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -1,2 +1,9 @@
 /* export-ignore
 /README-github_gitlab-autogenerated-archives.txt -export-ignore
+
+# strace-appimage: the derived patch series quotes diff context (lines
+# starting with a space before tab-indented code) and experiments/logs/
+# hold captured tool output (LD_DEBUG, configure, make); both legitimately
+# contain what the whitespace checker flags, so exempt them from it.
+patches/series/*.patch -whitespace
+experiments/logs/** -whitespace
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 0b0701787..b4cfc9222 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -46,7 +46,10 @@ jobs:
       - name: upload coverage
         uses: codecov/codecov-action@fb8b3582c8e4def4969c97caa2f19720cb33a72f	# v7.0.0
         with:
-          fail_ci_if_error: true
+          # strace-appimage: this repository is not registered on Codecov,
+          # so the OIDC upload answers "Repository not found"; keep the
+          # coverage build useful without failing the job on the upload.
+          fail_ci_if_error: false
           use_oidc: true
           plugins: gcov
           working-directory: src
